  "handoff": {
    "summary": "Added a separate source-transparent IntegerBuffer kernel for the exact outward-dyadic arithmetic in the Belabas--Friedman finite term. Directed mpmath/libmp transcendental endpoints and the existing coefficient kernel are unchanged. The host packs exact 2^-p mantissas, invokes one native or Wasm-compatible kernel crossing, reconstructs the same rigorous RealBall provenance, and falls back to the ordinary scalar implementation when the kernel boundary is unavailable or rejects storage. Differential tests compare the complete RealBall.to_dict payload across 64, 96, 128, 160, and 256-bit precision and exercise the unavailable-kernel fallback. For x^3-x^2-6*x-12 at 128 bits, threshold 13455 and 973 aggregated terms, the exact full payload matched while finite-term construction fell from 7.737 seconds scalar to 3.854 seconds packed and analytic-index measured 5.631 seconds versus the prior 8.634-second profile.",
    "risks": [
      "The kernel does not evaluate logarithms or square roots and does not widen the proof boundary: those endpoints remain rigorous exact rationals produced by mpmath.libmp directed rounding.",
      "Native compilation removes the interval-object arithmetic but not the roughly 3.6 seconds of transcendental endpoint generation, so native and ordinary same-source packed timings are close on this cubic.",
      "The local WASI GMP toolchain was unavailable, so the production-pack emitter and bridge inventory were validated but the end-to-end Wasm execution test remained environment-skipped.",
      "Central integration must regenerate packages/flint-wasm/release/production-kernel-coverage.json for the compiled-function count change from 229 to 230 and raise the number-field-global-arithmetic source budget above the measured 911609 bytes."
    ],
    "next_steps": [
      "Regenerate the production Wasm coverage/capability artifacts after cherry-picking; the expected compiled function count is 230 and the zeta production family has two functions.",
      "Run the full architecture and production-Wasm gates after the central package-budget and generated-coverage updates."
    ]
  }
